  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilient Journalism in the Digital Age</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &quot;Resilient Journalism in the Digital Age: Strengthening the fortitude of journalists and youth in Morocco in the face of online disinformation and digital threats&quot; is a three year project between the Norwegian Embassy in Rabat and UNESCO. The main outcome of the project is to enable media institutions and journalists in Morocco to be more resilient to online disinformation and digital threats and to develop a culture of safety for journalists which is crucial for a healthy democratic society in Morocco especially in the context of the increase in disinformation and emergence of artificial intelligence.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   

Impact: Create a culture of safety for journalists, youth and media institutions in Morocco that are more resilient to online disinformation and digital threats.                                                                                   
Outcomes: Media institutions and journalists in Morocco are more resilient to online disinformation and digital threats and a culture of safety for journalists is developed. 
Outputs: Women and men journalists and youth in Morocco have increased competency in media and information literacy and artificial intelligence including on countering disinformation and misinformation as well as online threats and harassment. Media institutions in Morocco have strengthened policy in place against threats and online harassments.</narrative>
  </description>
